1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,290
Each animal wants different stones.

2
00:00:02,610 --> 00:00:05,767
Let's meet the first three: Rabbit, Turtle and Salmon.

3
00:00:06,799 --> 00:00:08,122
This is the Rabbit.

4
00:00:08,442 --> 00:00:11,493
The Rabbit wants three stones, each a different color.

5
00:00:13,549 --> 00:00:14,744
Red, then blue.

6
00:00:15,064 --> 00:00:16,301
No points yet.

7
00:00:18,183 --> 00:00:19,185
Then yellow.

8
00:00:19,505 --> 00:00:20,892
Three different colors!

9
00:00:21,212 --> 00:00:22,428
That's six points.

10
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:26,050
The Rabbit only scores when all three are there.

11
00:00:27,166 --> 00:00:28,382
Next, the Turtle.

12
00:00:28,702 --> 00:00:31,774
The Turtle wants stones that are all the same color.

13
00:00:33,649 --> 00:00:34,908
One green stone.

14
00:00:35,228 --> 00:00:36,188
One point.

15
00:00:38,249 --> 00:00:39,636
Three green stones.

16
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:41,023
Six points.

17
00:00:43,083 --> 00:00:44,533
Five green stones.

18
00:00:44,853 --> 00:00:46,027
Fourteen points!

19
00:00:46,347 --> 00:00:47,947
More stones, more points.

20
00:00:49,066 --> 00:00:50,197
Now the Salmon.

21
00:00:50,517 --> 00:00:52,885
The Salmon is the opposite of the Turtle.

22
00:00:53,205 --> 00:00:55,338
Every stone must be a different color.

23
00:00:57,616 --> 00:00:58,981
Three different colors.

24
00:00:59,301 --> 00:01:00,325
Four points.

25
00:01:02,583 --> 00:01:03,884
All six colors.

26
00:01:04,204 --> 00:01:05,378
Thirteen points!

27
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,038
A tip: the last stones are worth the most.

28
00:01:09,358 --> 00:01:11,171
So try to fill your animals up.

29
00:01:12,299 --> 00:01:13,195
Remember.

30
00:01:13,515 --> 00:01:16,758
The Rabbit wants three different colors, for six points.

31
00:01:17,078 --> 00:01:18,956
The Turtle wants all one color.

32
00:01:19,275 --> 00:01:21,430
The Salmon wants all different colors.

33
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:23,670
Next: the Owl and the Beaver.
